chain.task:
Implement this task as the sole implementer: {task}

Plan: {outputs.plan}

Open and read the referenced plan, verify its critical assumptions against source, real consumers or dispatchers, and owning tests, then implement only the approved scope. Drop unnecessary files and stop if a contradiction materially changes that scope. Scope and refine searches when results are broad or truncated. If a pi-workbench-feature-ledger is referenced, open it, work only on the named stable ID, keep at most one task in-progress, and update its status, Evidence, and Handoff from the actual post-mutation state; never mark it done without fresh verification. Mark it blocked and stop if evidence invalidates the plan instead of widening scope. For a bug, reproduce narrowly when safe or confirm the causal trace before editing. Follow the plan's evidence strategy: witness a focused regression or contract test fail for the intended reason when feasible, use characterization coverage for risky refactors, and do not manufacture tests for prose or mechanical configuration. After the last mutation, run fresh focused validation, broaden it in proportion to blast radius, and inspect the current diff. Never weaken an assertion merely to make checks pass. Do not commit or push. Return a compact Markdown handoff with artifact path and stable ID when present, final state, changes, fresh command outcomes, decisions, next ready task, limitations, and residual risks; omit empty ceremony for a small change.

parallel.task:
Review the implementation for specification compliance, correctness, causal validity, integration, runtime, error, cleanup, cancellation, ordering, and concurrency defects.

Task: {task}
Plan: {outputs.plan}
Implementation handoff: {outputs.implementation}

Open and read every referenced artifact, including any pi-workbench-feature-ledger and sources named by its Spec baseline, and treat all claims as untrusted. Scope and refine broad or truncated searches. Review the named stable task, milestone, or gate against its acceptance criteria and verify that work-plan status, Evidence, and Handoff match the actual diff, source, callers, tests, and configuration. Trace every changed cross-boundary value through its real consumer or dispatcher, including code outside the diff, and check the owning test. For bug fixes, verify the causal seam; for refactors, verify stated invariants. Report only actionable defects introduced or exposed by this scope and tied to a violated contract; reject unrelated issues, speculation, preferences, optional hardening, and duplicate symptoms. Do not edit files. Finish with the required structured envelope: READY requires no findings; NOT_READY requires one or more findings. Keep evidence and residual risks compact, and include ledgerDisposition only for a named work-plan gate.

Review the implementation for missing regression or characterization coverage, stale or weak validation evidence, unnecessary complexity, maintainability regressions, and security issues only where a real trust boundary applies.

