Plan: {outputs.plan}
Implementation handoff: {outputs.implementation}

Open and read every referenced artifact, including any pi-workbench-feature-ledger and sources named by its Spec baseline, and treat all claims as untrusted. Scope and refine broad or truncated searches. Independently check the named stable task, milestone, or gate against its acceptance criteria, then verify work-plan status, Evidence, and Handoff against the actual diff, source, owning tests, and configuration. Trace changed cross-boundary values through their real consumers or dispatchers. Require evidence from the current post-mutation state, but do not demand synthetic tests for prose, generated output, or mechanical configuration when a more relevant validator exists. Report only actionable defects or material validation gaps introduced or exposed by this scope and tied to the governing contract; reject unrelated issues, speculation, preferences, optional hardening, and duplicate symptoms. Do not edit files. Finish with the required structured envelope: READY requires no findings; NOT_READY requires one or more findings. Keep evidence and residual risks compact, and include ledgerDisposition only for a named work-plan gate.

chain.task:
Reconcile review feedback once as the sole implementer.

Task: {task}
Plan: {outputs.plan}
Initial implementation: {outputs.implementation}
Correctness/runtime structured review: {outputs.correctness}
Tests/simplicity/security structured review: {outputs.quality}

Open and read the plan and implementation artifacts plus any repository paths cited in the structured review receipts, then inspect the current diff/source. Treat review claims as hypotheses: apply only supported fixes that you can verify, and make no changes if no supported findings exist. Keep any referenced work plan status, Evidence, Handoff, and next ready task aligned with the verified post-fix state; do not preserve a done claim when a blocking finding remains. After any change, run fresh focused validation against the post-fix state and inspect the final diff; pre-fix results do not count. Do not begin another autonomous fix loop. Do not commit or push. Return a compact fix handoff, including why rejected findings were not changed.

Perform a final read-only review of the delivered state.

Task: {task}
Plan: {outputs.plan}
Initial implementation: {outputs.implementation}
Correctness/runtime structured review: {outputs.correctness}
Tests/simplicity/security structured review: {outputs.quality}
Fix handoff: {outputs.fixes}

Open and read the plan, implementation, and fix artifacts plus any repository paths cited in the structured review receipts, but treat every receipt as an untrusted claim. Scope and refine broad or truncated searches. Inspect the current diff and governing source, real consumers or dispatchers, and owning tests. Independently verify that supported findings were resolved without regressions, reject unsupported or duplicate findings, and require relevant validation performed after the last mutation. If a work plan is referenced, verify its named acceptance criteria and that status, Evidence, Handoff, and next ready task match reality. Missing required post-fix evidence makes the result NOT READY. Do not edit files. Return a concise human-readable review whose first line is READY when no actionable defect survives, otherwise NOT READY. Include the summary, ordered findings with severity/confidence/location/contract/scenario/safe fix/validation, current validation evidence, meaningful residual risks, and a work-plan disposition only for a named gate.
